# Reference Playbooks

This repo follows three senior iOS playbooks vendored under `docs/playbooks/`.

## Before architectural or feature work

1. Read `memory/activeContext.md` and `memory/progress.md` (session state; see `agent-memory.mdc`)
2. Read `AGENTS.md` (Phase Gate Protocol)
3. Read `docs/playbooks/GamesLibrary-adaptations.md` (project-specific overrides)
4. Read the relevant playbook when you need deeper context:
   - `docs/playbooks/hexagonal-architecture.md` — ports, adapters, DI
   - `docs/playbooks/spec-driven-development.md` — SDD, SPEC.md, tests
   - `docs/playbooks/senior-ios-developer.md` — security, coordinator, previews

## Priority when docs conflict

`specs/<feature>/SPEC.md` → `GamesLibrary-adaptations.md` → `.cursor/rules/` → playbooks → generic examples in playbooks.

## Skills

Use `.cursor/skills/sdd-feature/` and `.cursor/skills/hexagonal-ios/` for this repo’s workflows. For SwiftUI/SDK 27/Swift Testing, use the Apple Xcode 27 skills in `.cursor/skills/` (`swiftui-specialist`, `swiftui-whats-new-27`, `modernize-tests`, …). Hexagonal + this adaptations file win on architecture.
